e has a different shape and  different dominant colors for example P3  DCI which is used for Cinema has a  predominance in the blue tones while a  white gamut will have a tendency towards  the green Hues so by using the color  space transform you can translate your  footage into different color spaces and  that will require subtle adjustments to  the power braid no worries it's nothing  difficult and I'll show you exactly how  most problems happen between the yellow  to Green transition or the blue pink  colors generally speaking I would say  these are the ugliest colors if I can  label them as that maybe it's a harsh  label or at least the most problematic  from the whole visible spectrum  it's very easy to get these colors to  look unattractive so many companies  choose to shift them or to saturate them  to render better colors  for example most Canon cameras I've  created so far have this tendency to  desaturate yellow and magenta pretty  heavily which is the perfect recipe for  pleasing skin tones  natural skin tones are not always the  most attractive looking and that is  because they have a lot of green yellow  magenta tones hot pinks and micro flaws  so just by working with these colors you  can actually get perfect skin tones very  easily next time you color gray skin  tones remember these details and you  will notice a huge Improvement in skin  color rendition just by doing a couple  simple steps interesting fact yellow  magenta don't even exist or at least our  eyes gonna see them because our eyes can  only capture shades of red green and  blue  so yellow magenta are actually brain  generated I guess to fill in the space  between the main colors that we see  which is pretty cool if you think about  it but these are the colors that will  give us most problems in color grading  and we might not even know it so if  you're having some color separation  between these colors I'll show you  exactly what to do and don't worry it's  very simple all you have to do g